                <pb facs="0733" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg605"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 452.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Buck</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 30,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 129, of May
                    29th last, I have to ask that you will report in the case of Owen Young, the
                    American citizen, whose assassin, notwithstanding the vigorous action of the
                    late minister at Lima, had not at last accounts been arrested. Meantime you will
                    please refer to the correspondence in the case and press the subject of the
                    assassin’s arrest. * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
